From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:45:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6apm-dai: queue no playback buffers while
 stopped

q6apm_dai_ack() sends a buffer to the DSP for every period userspace
writes, also after TRIGGER_STOP, which leaves the DSP graph running.
After a speaker protection fault tore down the WSA back end, with
userspace preparing again at once, about 50 buffers were refused with
-EBUSY within 170 ms because the GPR channel to the ADSP was full, and
the ADSP then answered no more commands until reboot.

Queue buffers only while the stream is not stopped, as q6asm-dai does.
A start after a stop without a prepare, which ALSA allows after a
failed start, sends what was written meanwhile; for that the queue
pointer is reset by prepare instead of stop, which also keeps such a
start from resending the periods before the stop.

Tested with the fault held for 1 s and for 150 s: no buffer was refused
and the speakers played again once the fault cleared.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c | 22 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
index 725b0ac0c3e4..032dfbab09aa 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
@@ -398,6 +398,7 @@ static int q6apm_dai_prepare(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 	}
 
 	prtd->last_pos_index = 0;
+	prtd->queue_ptr = 0;
 	prtd->pcm_count = snd_pcm_lib_period_bytes(substream);
 	if (q6apm_is_graph_in_push_pull_mode(prtd->graph)) {
 		if (prtd->pcm_size != prtd->push_pull_size) {
@@ -475,6 +476,14 @@ static int q6apm_dai_ack(struct snd_soc_component *component, struct snd_pcm_sub
 	if (!prtd->graph || q6apm_is_graph_in_push_pull_mode(prtd->graph))
 		return 0;
 
+	/*
+	 * A stopped stream queues no buffers: its graph may feed a back end
+	 * that is gone, and the buffers would pile up in the DSP until it takes
+	 * no more commands.
+	 */
+	if (prtd->state != Q6APM_STREAM_RUNNING)
+		return 0;
+
 	if (substream->stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK) {
 		avail_periods = (runtime->control->appl_ptr - prtd->queue_ptr)/runtime->period_size;
 		for (i = 0; i < avail_periods; i++) {
@@ -501,11 +510,22 @@ static int q6apm_dai_trigger(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 	case SNDRV_PCM_TRIGGER_START:
 	case SNDRV_PCM_TRIGGER_RESUME:
 	case SNDRV_PCM_TRIGGER_PAUSE_RELEASE:
+		/*
+		 * Started again without a prepare, e.g. after a failed start:
+		 * send what was written while stopped.
+		 */
+		if (prtd->state == Q6APM_STREAM_STOPPED) {
+			prtd->state = Q6APM_STREAM_RUNNING;
+			ret = q6apm_dai_ack(component, substream);
+			if (ret < 0)
+				prtd->state = Q6APM_STREAM_STOPPED;
+			else
+				ret = 0;
+		}
 		break;
 	case SNDRV_PCM_TRIGGER_STOP:
 		/* TODO support be handled via SoftPause Module */
 		prtd->state = Q6APM_STREAM_STOPPED;
-		prtd->queue_ptr = 0;
 		prtd->last_pos_index = 0;
 		break;
 	case SNDRV_PCM_TRIGGER_SUSPEND:
